COMP2000 SIMULATION PROJECT - AARON PANG 49071378

This project aims to demonstrate the object-oriented programming practices described in COMP2000.

The simulation is a small meadow containing a number of different plants, which grow and spread
in different ways depending on the time of day, weather, and other types of plants around.

Plants can be added to "Patch"es of their type, which are groups that are more fertile than
other plants. These are currently represented with a square border on the ground.

Sunflowers begin as small seeds and grow larger, represented by yellow boxes. They spread in a
radius around themselves.

Weeds are small but grow and spread fast in a single direction. Individal plants are small and
have a linear growth pattern.
